# text
seg-4263435e702a = Section { "5.2" } (Prevent, Respond, Recover)

# text
seg-e7b721f6e216 = Resilience is described as three functions: preventing harm, responding (detect, report, mitigate, contain) and recovering. Detection is probabilistic, so false alarms and missed detections both matter.

# text
seg-3447d3b53fe8 = Receiver-log trust assessment; Spoofing and meaconing detection; Holdover and coasting

# text
seg-ab055a50e16e = Prevention is a product-design property that no simulation output shows. Detection statistics from a synthetic or single-session run are not a measured false-alarm or miss rate for a fielded product.

# text
seg-501badd6a436 = Level { "1" }, requirement { "1" }

# text
seg-e8cfbe121084 = Check that stored data arriving from external sources matches the formats and value ranges of the relevant standards.

# text
seg-fdbb9db68f1d = none

# text
seg-7d7196aefa05 = A software-assurance and input-validation property of the product under test. Kshana does not inspect a product's input handling.

# text
seg-6085030de980 = Level { "1" }, requirement { "2" }

# text
seg-e8cd6fb732ad = Allow full manual recovery by clearing or resetting memory, returning the system to defined performance once the threat is gone.

# text
seg-8d216d42c776 = Receiver-log trust assessment

# text
seg-e3ca721d9d2e = A receiver log shows when a fix became untrusted and when it recovered; it does not show that a manual reset clears every stored state.

# text
seg-2c78c15cea96 = Level { "1" }, requirement { "3" }

# text
seg-ab9458f8b8fc = Reload or update firmware securely.

# text
seg-3a50eceb47f5 = Firmware update security is outside what any Kshana output observes.

# text
seg-752a194674f6 = Level { "2" }, requirement { "4" }

# text
seg-a5f263a083c7 = Identify compromised PNT sources and stop them corrupting the solution.

# text
seg-4e7034acccc0 = Spoofing and meaconing detection; Receiver-log trust assessment; Integrity monitoring and protection levels

# text
seg-d5fdef2a78f2 = Kshana scores detectors and monitors it models or runs over a log; whether a product's own source exclusion works needs the product's internal state, not only its log.

# text
seg-e3ea1208fac9 = Level { "2" }, requirement { "5" }

# text
seg-c0219254fe8e = Recover sources and the system automatically without interrupting output; a solution is still provided during the threat, with possibly unbounded degradation.

# text
seg-3dd48cb65cb4 = Holdover and coasting; Receiver-log trust assessment

# text
seg-0c36c4a3eb4e = Holdover runs bound modelled drift for a stated clock or inertial model, not the product's own recovery behaviour.

# text
seg-befbf4b94876 = Level { "3" }, requirement { "6" }

# text
seg-45410d1675be = Corrupt data from one source must not contaminate another source.

# text
seg-ff808ce8ec48 = Alternative and diverse PNT sources

# text
seg-ccf628643110 = Kshana runs sources side by side; source isolation inside a product needs design review or fault injection into the product.

# text
seg-a1d5a3125697 = Level { "3" }, requirement { "7" }

# text
seg-db149ea618dd = Cross-verify the solutions of all sources, and keep degradation during a threat bounded.

# text
seg-4afa05ef42fa = Integrity monitoring and protection levels; Holdover and coasting; Alternative and diverse PNT sources

# text
seg-8b1f938c0175 = Bounded degradation is shown for the modelled sensors; the product's own cross-checking is not observed.

# text
seg-772244881e5b = Level { "4" }, requirement { "8" }

# text
seg-aff5161e6363 = Use sources of different technologies against common-mode threats, with no degradation during the threat.

# text
seg-587889f9881c = Alternative and diverse PNT sources; Jamming link-budget effects

# text
seg-65b96caf8d6b = A common-mode argument needs the real product's source set and a threat that spans them; a scenario states one, it does not prove the product has no shared weakness.

# text
seg-3c4cc0793454 = Section { "5.5" } (common mode)

# text
seg-a87c9808dd99 = Diverse mechanisms must not share a weakness: for example a jammer that covers two bands defeats band diversity.

# text
seg-c10ba3bb01be = Jamming link-budget effects; Resilience scoring over threat ensembles; Alternative and diverse PNT sources

# text
seg-843fe2fc9e33 = Scoring uses a synthetic threat ensemble, stated as such; it is not field data.

# text
seg-3158e7efd1a5 = Sections { "8.1" } to { "8.3" } (evaluation)

# text
seg-3942d9cdc64b = Evaluation combines static analysis with dynamic analysis, where test vectors stand in for threats; the test classes are source failure, interference and internal faults. Simulators are named as a test method.

# text
seg-9d5c297c1ab9 = Receiver-log trust assessment; Jamming link-budget effects; Spoofing and meaconing detection

# text
seg-bb02568e8f8f = Exported motion and events can drive a laboratory simulator (docs/TEST-BENCH.md). Kshana writes no signal, so the simulator and its authorised operator supply the threat.

# text
seg-b81625e9e071 = Section { "8.6" } (test-plan elements)

# text
seg-27d645a79672 = A test plan states the level, requirement, inputs, references, data access needed, procedure with pass or fail criteria, results and notes.

# text
seg-1f2898855ccc = Reproducible run provenance; Receiver-log trust assessment

# text
seg-d8b08da48cb2 = Pass or fail criteria are chosen by the assessor; Kshana records the inputs, thresholds and hashes it ran with.

